Column name: neumann_class Type: TEXT Description: EX - Extratropical TC - Tropical MM - Missing
Column name: reunion_rmw Type: NUMBER Description: Radius of maximum winds
Column name: hko_longitude Type: FLOAT Description: Longitude from Hong Kong Observatory
Column name: reunion_r64_se Type: NUMBER Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: name Type: TEXT Description: Name provided by the agency. IBTrACS ignores most names that include digits or abbreviations.
Column name: tokyo_r50_dir Type: NUMBER Description: 1 : Northeast (NE)  2 : East (E)  3 : Southeast (SE)  4 : South (S)  5 : Southwest (SW)  6 : West (W)  7 : Northwest (NW)  8 : North (N)  9 : (symmetric circle)
Column name: usa_wind Type: NUMBER Description: Maximum sustained wind speed in knots: 0 - 300 kts.
Column name: newdelhi_grade Type: TEXT Description: Types of disturbances: Low pressure area W<17 knots D - Depression 17<=W<28 DD - Deep Depression 28<=W<34 CS - Cyclonic Storm 34<=W<48 SCS - Severe Cyclonic Storm 48<=W<64 VSCS - Very Severe Cyclonic Storm 64<=W<120 SCS - Super Cyclonic Storm W>=120 knots
Column name: td9635_roci Type: NUMBER Description: Size. (Radius of system)
Column name: bom_wind Type: NUMBER Description: This is the estimated maximum mean wind around the cyclone – that is in the vicinity of the centre.
Column name: reunion_ci Type: FLOAT Description: Dvorak CI-number
Column name: reunion_type Type: NUMBER Description: 01= tropics; disturbance ( no closed isobars)  02= <34 knot winds/n<17m/s winds and at least one closed isobar  03= 34-63 knots/n17-32m/s  04= >63 knots/n>32m/s  05= extratropical  06= dissipating  07= subtropical cyclone (nonfrontal/nlow pressure system that comprises  initially baroclinic circulation developing over subtropical water)  08= overland  09= unknown
Column name: mlc_latitude Type: FLOAT Description: Latitude from Mike Chenoweth data with updated data for the North Atlantic for the 1800s.
Column name: tokyo_land Type: NUMBER Description: <Indicator of landfall or passage>  Landfall or passage over the Japanese islands occurred within  one hour after the time of the analysis with this indicator.
Column name: bom_rmw Type: NUMBER Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the maximum mean wind.
Column name: usa_sshs Type: NUMBER Description: Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Scale information based on the wind speed provided by the US agency wind speed (US agencies provide 1-minute wind speeds) -5 = Unknown [XX] -4 = Post-tropical [EX/nET/nPT] -3 = Miscellaneous disturbances [WV/nLO/nDB/nDS/nIN/nMD] -2 = Subtropical [SS/nSD] Tropical systems classified based on wind speeds [TD/nTS/nHU/nTY,/nTC/nST/nHR]  -1 = Tropical depression (W<34)  0 = Tropical storm [34<W<64]  1 = Category 1 [64<=W<83]  2 = Category 2 [83<=W<96]  3 = Category 3 [96<=W<113]  4 = Category 4 [113<=W<137]  5 = Category 5 [W >= 137]
Column name: reunion_r50_nw Type: NUMBER Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: wellington_pressure Type: NUMBER
Column name: bom_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: Central pressure of the cyclone
Column name: td9635_pressure Type: NUMBER
Column name: tokyo_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: Central pressure
Column name: nadi_cat Type: NUMBER Description: Nadi assigned category
Column name: td9636_stage Type: NUMBER Description: This field gives an estimate of the highest winds occurring in the storm at the time and location indicated. The entire storm was coded as to the highest stage reached for some of the earlier years. 0 - Tropical disturbance (1969 onward) 1 - depression < 34 [some variation in definition for S Indian] 2 - Storm 34-63 [with some variation in definition for S Indian] 3 - point where wind reached 64 knots [except N Indian where it is wind 43-47 knots] 4 - Hurricane > 64 [except in N Indian/nWind > 48] 5 - Extratropical 6 - Dissipating 7 - Unknown Intensity or doubtful track
Column name: tokyo_r30_dir Type: NUMBER Description: 1 : Northeast (NE)  2 : East (E)  3 : Southeast (SE)  4 : South (S)  5 : Southwest (SW)  6 : West (W)  7 : Northwest (NW)  8 : North (N)  9 : (symmetric circle)
Column name: number Type: NUMBER Description: The cardinal number of the system for that season. The count includes all basins/nso this will not be continuous for basin files.
Column name: newdelhi_wind Type: NUMBER
Column name: bom_r50_nw Type: NUMBER Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Northwest quadrant.
